{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:15:39.140Z","data":{"text":"Done. The replay test passes on the first run, confirming tasks 1 and 2 already match TypeScript's merge.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Changed:** `crates/kernel/specs/tests/replay_corpus.rs` — a corpus test proving rust-specs \"Living specs replay\". It:\n- Walks `openspec/changes/archive/` in landing order (eventless folders first by name bytes, then by the last `archived` event's string `timestamp`, then by name), then active changes holding `.run/archive-specs.json`.\n- Merges each folder with `merge_change` into an empty scratch specs folder under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, writing each merged text or removing the capability folder before the next; a merge error panics naming the folder and error.\n- Checks every capability with a living folder or replayed delta: absent replay ↔ absent living `spec.md`, the six named capabilities after reading their first `## Purpose\\n\\n` as `## Purpose\\n`, and exact equality for all others; it also fails any six that matches without the transform. All failures (each with its first differing line) are collected before asserting.\n\n**Result:** `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --test replay_corpus -- --include-ignored` green; `cargo fmt --all` clean; workspace clippy clean; `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` passes.\n\n**Deviated:** No `replay_corpus_cases*.rs` was added — the acceptance conditions it on fixing a line in `src/merge/`, and the replay already matched with no such fix. Only the corpus test file (excluded from cargo-mutants) is in the diff, so the mutation step has no new source line to cover.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/218-rust-specs-merge/.run/results/3.md`."}}
